        <h3 style="font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:700;color:#0B1E38;margin:0 0 8px;">The 15-Minute Cake Thawing Rule</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#475569;line-height:1.6;margin:0;">
          DQ commercial freezers hold ice cream at -10°F. Slicing immediately causes the outer soft-serve shell to shatter and the chocolate cookie crunch layer to crumble. Rest your cake at room temperature for 15 minutes and wipe a hot-water-dipped knife between cuts for clean catering-quality slices.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background:#FAF7F2;border:1px solid #EDE4D6;border-radius:16px;padding:24px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(11,30,56,0.04);">
